{"name":"Cinema Screen","hex":"#95878e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cinema","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A movie theatre, a movie house.","Films collectively."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cinema"},{"term":"screen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A physical barrier that shelters or hides.\nA physical divider intended to block an area from view, or provide shelter from something dangerous.","A physical divider intended to block an area from view, or provide shelter from something dangerous."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To filter by passing through a screen.","To filter."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/screen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Projection screen","blocks":[{"text":"A projection screen is an installation consisting of a surface and a support structure used for displaying a projected image for the view of an audience. Projection screens may be permanently installed on a wall, as in a movie theater, mounted to or placed in a ceiling using a rollable projection surface that retracts into a casing, painted on a wall, or portable with tripod or floor rising models as in a conference room or other non-dedicated viewing space. Another popular type of portable screens are inflatable screens for outdoor movie screening."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Sala_de_cine.jpg/330px-Sala_de_cine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Projection_screen"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Projection-screen-home2.jpg/500px-Projection-screen-home2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Projection-screen-home2.jpg/1280px-Projection-screen-home2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thu